========================================================================================
1a. StatevectorEstimator(default_precision=p) semantics
========================================================================================
  precision=0.011049 -> measured std 0.010491   ratio std/precision = 0.950
  precision=0.050000 -> measured std 0.050812   ratio std/precision = 1.016
  precision=0.200000 -> measured std 0.204664   ratio std/precision = 1.023
  Var(H) at this point = 12.0278
  If std == precision for every p, the estimator ADDS FIXED NOISE and is
  blind to Var(H) - it is not simulating shots.

========================================================================================
1b/2. Per-problem: effective shots the baselines receive, and G
========================================================================================
  nominal SHOTS = 8192, PRECISION = 0.011049

  problem            terms    G    Var(H)   G*sumVar   eff shots   subsidy  circ x
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  H2                     5    2     0.185      0.373        3059        0x      2x
  LiH                   15    3     0.159      0.488        3995        0x      3x
  Heisenberg N=4         9    3     8.315     23.356      191331       23x      3x
  Heisenberg N=6        15    3    14.110     42.957      351902       43x      3x
  Heisenberg N=8        21    3    21.241     56.726      464701       57x      3x
  MaxCut N=4             4    1     0.766      0.766        6278        1x      1x
  MaxCut N=6            11    1     3.977      3.977       32580        4x      1x

  eff shots = G * sum_g Var(H_g) / PRECISION^2 : what a real device needs
  to deliver the standard error the baselines are being GIVEN for free.
  subsidy = that, over the 8192 the benchmark claims to be enforcing.
  circ x  = factor by which baseline circuit counts are UNDERCOUNTED.

  subsidy range 0x - 57x, median 4x
  G range 1 - 3

  DIRECTION OF BIAS: both defects flatter the BASELINES and penalise V3,
  which samples real shots and needs one setting. Fixing them can only
  improve V3's standing, so the published 180-vs-320-1360 comparison is
  CONSERVATIVE, not inflated. V2 sits on the subsidised path, so the
  V2-vs-V3 comparisons in RESULT are the ones actually at risk.
